hadiths[73]{hadithnumber,text}:
"544","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Hakam al-Warraq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, that Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \I travelled with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"
"545","Abu An-Nadrah said:\Imran bin Husain was asked about the traveler's prayer. He said: 'I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah"""""
"546","Anas bin Malik narrated:\We prayed Zuhr as four with the Prophet in Al-Madinah"""""
"547","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet went from Al-Madinah to Makkah"""""
"548","Yahya bin Abi Ishaq Al-Hadrami narrated :that Anas bin Malik said: \We went with the Messenger of Allah from Al-Madinah to Makkah"""""
"549","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah traveled on a journey and he prayed two Rak'ah for nineteen days.\"" Ibn Abbas said: \""So when we would stay somewhere for nineteen (days) we would pray two Rak'ah"""""
"550","Al-Bara bin Azib said:\I accompanied the Messenger of Allah on eighteen journeys"""""
"551","Ibn Umar narrated:\I prayed Zuhr with the Prophet on a journey as two Rak'ah"""""
"552","**Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaid al-Muḥārībī al-Kūfī narrated to us, saying:** ʿAlī ibn Hāshim narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAṭiyyah and Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with both of them), who said:\n\n\I prayed with the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam) both while resident and while travelling. I prayed with him while resident: Ẓuhr as four rakʿāt"
"553","Mu'adh bin Jabal narrated:""While the Prophet as at the Battle of Tabuk, if he wanted to depart before the sun's decline he would delay Zuhr so that he could pray it together with Asr. If he wanted to depart after the sun's decline, he would hasten Asr to Zuhr, and pray Zuhr and Asr together, and then move it. If he wanted to depart before Maghrib he would delay Maghrib until he prayed it with Isha, and if he wanted to depart after Maghrib he would hasten Isha so that he would pray it along with Maghrib"
"554","Abd al-Samad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Zakariyya al-Lu'lu'i narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-A'yan narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, and Qutaybah narrated this Hadith, meaning the Hadith of Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him). The Hadith of Mu'adh is a Hasan Gharib Hadith; Qutaybah is the sole narrator of it, and we do not know of anyone other than him who narrated it from al-Layth. The Hadith of al-Layth from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Tufayl from Mu'adh is a Gharib Hadith. What is well-known among the scholars is the Hadith of Mu'adh as narrated by Abu al-Zubayr from Abu al-Tufayl from Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) combined, during the expedition of Tabuk, between Dhuhr and 'Asr, and between Maghrib and 'Isha'. This was narrated by Qurrah ibn Khalid, Sufyan al-Thawri, Malik, and others from Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki. It is with reference to this Hadith that Imam al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) issued his ruling. Ahmad and Ishaq (may Allah have mercy on them both) stated: \There is no harm in combining the two prayers during travel in the time of either one of them.\"""""""
"555","Nafi narrated:\Ibn Umar had been requested to urgently attend to one of his wives"""""
"556","Abbad bin Tamim narrated from his uncle:\The Messenger of Allah went out with the people to seek rain. So he led them in prayer for two Rak'ah"""""
"557","Qutaybah narrated to us, who said: Layth ibn Sa‘d narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa‘id ibn Abi Hilal, from Yazid ibn ‘Abdullah, from ‘Umays, the freedman of Abu al-Laham, from Abu al-Laham, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) at the stones of oil, praying for rain, raising his palms in supplication. Abu ‘Isa said: Qutaybah said this in the hadith from Abu al-Laham, and we do not know of any other hadith from the Prophet (peace be upon him) from him except this one. ‘Umays, the freedman of Abu al-Laham, narrated other hadiths from the Prophet (peace be upon him) and was a Companion."
"558","It is narrated from Hisham bin Ishaq - and he was from Ibn Abdullah bin Kinanah - from his father who said:\Al-Walid bin Uqbah"""""
"559","(Another chain) from Hisham bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah, from his father, :and he mentioned a similar narration and added: ""with humility"" to it"
"560","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ that he prayed in an eclipse, so he recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed three times, then prostrated two prostrations, and the other one was like it. He said: In this chapter there are narrations from Ali, Aishah, Abd Allah ibn Amr, al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, Abu Mas'ud, Abu Bakrah, Samurah, Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, Ibn Mas'ud, Asma bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, Ibn Umar, Qabisah al-Hilali, Jabir ibn Abd Allah, Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, and Ubayy ibn Ka'b. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Ibn Abbas is hasan sahih. It has been narrated from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ that he prayed in an eclipse four rak'ahs in four prostrations. Al-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq hold this view. He said: The people of knowledge differed regarding recitation in the eclipse prayer. Some saw that one should recite silently in it during the day. Some saw that one should recite aloud in it, similar to the Eid and Jumu'ah prayers. Malik, Ahmad, and Ishaq hold this view, seeing the recitation aloud in it. Al-Shafi'i said: One does not recite aloud in it. Both narrations are authentic from the Prophet ﷺ: it is authentic that he prayed four rak'ahs in four prostrations, and it is also authentic that he prayed six rak'ahs in four prostrations. This is permissible according to the people of knowledge, according to the length of the eclipse: if the eclipse prolonged, he prayed six rak'ahs in four prostrations, it is permissible; if he prayed four rak'ahs in four prostrations and prolonged the recitation, it is permissible. Our companions see that the eclipse prayer should be performed in congregation for both solar and lunar eclipses."
"561","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in prayer. He prolonged the recitation, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then raised his head and prolonged the recitation, and it was shorter than the first. Then he bowed and prolonged the bowing, and it was shorter than the first. Then he raised his head and prostrated. Then he did the like of that in the second rak'ah. Abu Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. With this hadith, al-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq say: they see the eclipse prayer as four rak'ahs in four prostrations. Al-Shafi'i said: He recites in the first rak'ah with Umm al-Qur'an and the equivalent of Surat al-Baqarah silently if it is by day, then bows a long bowing equivalent to his recitation, then raises his head with takbir and stands as he is, and recites also with Umm al-Qur'an and the equivalent of Al Imran, then bows a long bowing equivalent to his recitation, then raises his head and says: ""Sami Allahu liman hamidah."" Then he prostrates two complete prostrations, and stays in each prostration equivalent to what he stayed in his bowing. Then he stands and recites with Umm al-Qur'an and the equivalent of Surat al-Nisa, then bows a long bowing equivalent to his recitation, then raises his head with takbir and stands, then recites the equivalent of Surat al-Ma'idah, then bows a long bowing equivalent to his recitation, then raises and says: ""Sami Allahu liman hamidah."" Then he prostrates two prostrations, then gives the tashahhud and salam."
"562","Samurah bin Jundah narrated:\The Prophet led us in prayer during an eclipse; we did not hear his voice"""""
"563","Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Abān narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Ṣadaqah narrated to us, from Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the eclipse prayer and recited aloud therein.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ḥadīth. Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī narrated a similar version from Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn. This hadith is the basis for the position of Mālik ibn Anas, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq."
"564","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ prayed the fear prayer with one of the two groups for one rak'ah, while the other group faced the enemy. Then they withdrew and stood in the place of those, and those came and he prayed with them another rak'ah, then gave salam upon them. Then these stood and completed their rak'ah, and those stood and completed their rak'ah. Abu Isa said: This is a sahih hadith. Musa ibn Uqbah narrated from Nafi from Ibn Umar the like of this. He said: In this chapter there are narrations from Jabir, Hudhayfah, Zayd ibn Thabit, Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayrah, Ibn Mas'ud, Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi (his name is Zayd ibn Samit), and Abu Bakrah. Abu Isa said: Malik ibn Anas went in the fear prayer to the hadith of Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, and it is the view of al-Shafi'i. Ahmad said: The fear prayer has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ in various forms, and I do not know in this chapter except a sahih hadith, and I choose the hadith of Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah. Thus said Ishaq ibn Ibrahim: The narrations from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the fear prayer are established. He saw that whatever is narrated from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the fear prayer is permissible, and this is according to the measure of the fear. Ishaq said: We do not choose the hadith of Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah over the other narrations."
"565","Sahl bin Abi Hathmah said about Salat Al-Khawf:\The Imam stands facing the Qiblah while a group of them stand with him"""""
"566","(Abu Eisa said:) Muhammad bin Bash-har said: \I asked Yahya bin Sa'eed (narrators in no. 565) about this Hadith. So he narrated it to me from Shu'bah"""""
"567","It was narrated by Mālik ibn Anas, from Yazīd ibn Rūmān, from Ṣāliḥ ibn Khawwāt, from one who performed the Prayer of Fear (*Ṣalāt al-Khawf*) with the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned something similar to the preceding narration. ""\nHe further stated: \""""Upon this position stand Mālik"""""
"568","Abu Ad-Darda narrated:\I performed eleven prostrations (of recitation) with the Messenger of Allah"""""
"569","(Another chain in which) Abu Ad-Darda narrated:\I performed eleven prostrations with the Messenger of Allah"""""
"570","**Narrated by Nusayr ibn 'Alī, who narrated from 'Īsā ibn Yūnus, from al-A'mash, from Mujāhid, who said:**\n\n\We were in the presence of Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them) when he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **'Permit the women to go to the mosques at night.'**\n\nThereupon"
"571","Tariq bin Abdullah Al-Muharibi narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \When you are in Salat then do not spit on your right"""""
"572","Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \To spit in the Masjid is a sin"""""
"573","Abu Hurairah narrated:\We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah in: 'Read! In the Name of your Lord' and 'When the heaven is split asunder"""""
"574","(Another chain in which) Abu Hurairah narrated :from the Prophet similarly"
"575","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah prostrated for it - meaning (in Surat) An-Najm - and so did the Muslims"""""
"576","Yahya ibn Musa narrated to us: Waki narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I recited al-Najm to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not prostrate in it. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Zayd ibn Thabit is hasan sahih. Some people of knowledge interpreted this hadith, saying: The Prophet ﷺ only left the prostration because when Zayd ibn Thabit recited, he did not prostrate, so the Prophet ﷺ did not prostrate. They said: The prostration is obligatory upon whoever hears it, so they did not permit leaving it. They said: If a man hears it while not in a state of wudu, then when he performs wudu, he prostrates. This is the view of Sufyan al-Thawri and the people of Kufa, and Ishaq holds this view. Some people of knowledge said: The prostration is only upon whoever intends to prostrate in it and seeks its virtue, and they permitted leaving it if he so wished. They cited as evidence the marfu hadith, the hadith of Zayd ibn Thabit, where he said: ""I recited al-Najm to the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not prostrate in it."" They said: If the prostration were obligatory, the Prophet ﷺ would not have left Zayd until he prostrated, and the Prophet ﷺ would have prostrated. They also cited the hadith of Umar: he recited a prostration verse on the minbar, descended and prostrated; then he recited it on the second Jumu'ah, and the people prepared to prostrate, so he said: ""It was not written upon us except that we wish."" So he did not prostrate, and they did not prostrate. A group of people of knowledge went to this. It is the view of al-Shafi'i and Ahmad."
"577","Ibn Abbas narrated:\I saw the Messenger of Allah prostrating for (Surat) Sad.\"" Ibn Abbas said: \""It is not one of the resolute prostrations"""""
"578","Uqbah bin Amir narrated:\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Surah Al-Hajj has been esteemed by two prostrations?' He said: 'Yes"""""
"579","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid said:Ibn Juraij said to me: O Hasan! Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid informed me that Ibn Abbas said: \A man came to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I had a dream at night while I was sleeping in which I was praying behind a tree"""""
"580","Aisha narrated:\When the Messenger of Allah would prostrate (for recitation of) the Qur'an"""""
"581","Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \Whoever slept"""""
"582","Abu Hurairah narrated:\Muhammad said: 'Does not the one who raises his head before the Imam fear that Allah will transform his head into a donkey's head?"""""
"583","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:'Mu'adh bin Jabal would pray Al-Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah"
"584","Anas bin Malik narrated:\When we prayed behind the Prophet in the midday heat"""""
"585","Jabir bin Samurah narrated:\When the Prophet prayed Fajr he would remain seated where he had prayed until the sun had risen"""""
"586","Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \Whoever prays Fajr in congregation"""""
"587","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah would glance toward the right and the left during Salat but he would not turn his neck to look behind him"""""
"588","Sa'eed bin Abi Hind narrated from some of the companions of Ikrimah:\The Prophet would glance during Salat\"" and he mentioned a similar narration"""""
"589","Anas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah said to me: 'O my son! Beware of looking around during the Salat"""""
"590","Aishah narrated:\I asked the Messenger of Allah about looking around during the Salat. He said: 'It is a portion which the Shaitan snatches during a man's prayer"""""
"591","Mu'adh bin Jabal narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \When one of you comes to the Salat and (finds) the Imam is in a position"""""
"592","Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah narrated from his father that :the Messenger of Allah said: \When the Iqamah is called for the prayer"""""
"593","**Chain of Narration:**\n\nMaḥmūd ibn Ghaylān narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us — from ʿĀṣim — from Zirr — from ʿAbdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\n**The Narration:**\n\nI was praying, and the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), along with Abū Bakr and ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with them both), were with him. When I sat [in the tashahhud], I began with extolling the praise of Allāh, then sending ṣalawāt upon the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), then I supplicated for myself. Thereupon the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said:\n\n> **\Ask"
"594","Aishah narrated:\The Prophet ordered the construction of Masajid in all Dur and that they be kept clean and scented"""""
"595","It was narrated to us by Hannad, it was narrated to us by Abdah and Waki', from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) commanded, and he mentioned something similar to it. Abu Isa said: This hadith is more authentic than the first hadith."
"596","Narrated to us was Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated to us was Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) commanded and mentioned something similar to it. Sufyan said: His statement, \with the construction of masjids in the houses"
"597","Ibn Umar narrated that :the Prophet said: \The Salat during the night and the day is two and two"""""
"598","Asim bin Damrah said:\We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah during the day. He said: 'You will not be able to do that.' We said: 'Whoever among is able (he will)?' So he said: 'When the sun appeared over there (east) like it appears here (west) at Asr"""""
"599","**Narrated by 'Alī (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar narration:**\n\nMuḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah reported to us, from Abū Isḥāq, from 'Āṣim ibn Ḍamrah, from 'Alī (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet ﷺ, a narration of similar import.\n\nAbū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: *\This is a ḥasan (good) hadith.\""*\n\nIsḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm said: *\""The finest narration that has been transmitted regarding the voluntary prayers of the Prophet ﷺ during the daytime is this one.\""*\n\nIt has been reported that 'Abdullāh ibn al-Mubārak used to consider this hadith as weak (ḍa'īf).\n\n**Reason for its weakness:** According to us — and Allah knows best — it was deemed weak because a narration of this nature is not reported from the Prophet ﷺ except through this particular chain"
"600","Aishah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah would not pray in women's covers"""""
"601","Urwah narrated that Aishah said:\I came while the Messenger of Allah was praying in the house and the door was closed. So he walked until he opened the door for me"""""
"602","Abu Wa'il said:\A man asked Abdullah bin Mas'ud about this phrase: 'Ghairi asin' or is it Yasin? So he said: 'You can recite all of the Quran besides this [phrase]?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Indeed a people recite it"""""
"603","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \When a man performs Wudu and he performs his Wudu well"""""
"604","Sa'd bin Ishaq bin Ka'b bin Ujrah narrated from his father from his grandfather who said:\The Prophet prayed Maghrib in the Masjid of Banu Abdul-Ashbal"""""
"605","Qais bin Asim narrated that:he accepted Islam and the Prophet ordered him to perform Ghusl with water and Sidr"
"606","Ali bin Abi Talid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \The screen between the eyes of the jinns and nakedness of the children of Adam when one of you enters the area of relieving oneself is saying: 'Bismillah"""""
"607","Abdullah bin Busr narrated that :the Prophet said: \On the day of Resurrection"""""
"608","Aishah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah would love to start with the right side when he purified himself"""""
"609","Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: The acceptable Wudu is with two Ratils of water"
"610","Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said"
"611","Shahr bin Hawshab said:\I saw Jarir bin Abdullah performing Wudu and wiping over his Khuff.\"" He said: \""So I asked him: 'What is that?' He said: 'I saw the Prophet performing Wudu and he wiped over his Khuff.' So I said to him: 'Before Al-Ma'idah or after Al-Ma'idah?' He said: 'I did not accept Islam until after Al-Ma'idah"""""
"612","Shahr bin Hawshab said:(Another chain) from Khalid bin Ziyad with similar"
"613","Ammar narrated:\The Prophet permitted the Junub when he wanted to eat"""""
"614","Ka'b bin Ujrah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah said to me: 'I seek refuge in Allah for you O Ka'b bin Ujrah from leader that will be after me. Whoever comes to their doors to approve of their lies and supports them in their oppression"""""
"615","Muhammad said:\Ibn Numair narrated to us from Ubaidullah bin Musa"""""
"616","Sulaim bin Amir narrated:\I heard Abu Umamah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah giving a Khutbah during the Farewell Hajj"""""
